Camellia server Debian packaging
================================

The Debian rules package three prebuilt, statically linked binaries. They do
not compile Rust source during the Debian build. This keeps release archives,
container images, and Debian packages tied to the same Cargo build artifact.

For a native local build:

  cargo build --locked --release --all-features
  install -Dm0755 target/release/hbbs bin/hbbs
  install -Dm0755 target/release/hbbr bin/hbbr
  install -Dm0755 target/release/rustdesk-utils bin/rustdesk-utils
  sed "s/{{ ARCH }}/$(dpkg --print-architecture)/" \
    debian/control.tpl > debian/control
  dpkg-buildpackage --build=binary --no-sign

The release workflow uses the same layout with architecture-specific binaries
produced by `cross`. Do not substitute a binary built for another Debian
architecture: the package metadata deliberately declares the target
architecture rather than `all`.

The hbbs unit is enabled by normal debhelper policy but has
`ConditionFileNotEmpty=/etc/default/camellia-server`; create and validate that
configuration before starting the service. See docs/environment-variables.md.
Persistent keys and the SQLite database live in /var/lib/rustdesk-server and
are intentionally preserved when either package is removed.
